{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanThreeBodyCluster","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanThreeBodyCluster","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu3_sign_compatible_with_borromean_cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu3_sign_compatible_with_borromean_cluster","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**Sign selection.**  The residual moment `μ₃ > 0` and the Borromean cluster\n`c₃ = E₀·(1 − τ_Borr) > 0` (physical regime) lie on the *same* strictly-positive\nside — so the Brunnian operator is sign-compatible with `μ₃`.  Contrast\n`Mu4RhoFCluster.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster`, where the `≤ 0` pairwise content\nis sign-*incompatible* with the same `μ₃`.  (This fixes the *sign* only; it makes\nno magnitude claim — `μ₃`'s value enters neither statement nor proof.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.borromean_cluster_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.borromean_cluster_pos","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L93-L98","doc":"**(LEAD, strict) `c₃ > 0` in the physical regime** (`E₀ > 0`, `q ≠ 1`).  So\nthe Borromean cluster is *sign-compatible* with `μ₃ > 0` — unlike any pairwise\ninterface product (`Mu4RhoFCluster.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.borromean_cluster_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.borromean_cluster_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**(LEAD) The Borromean irreducible 3-body cluster is non-negative.**  For a\nnon-negative energy scale `E₀`, the Brunnian binding cluster\n`c₃ = E₀·(1 − τ_Borr)` is `≥ 0` — the forward complement of\n`Mu4RhoFCluster.pairwise_3body_content_nonpos` (which is `≤ 0`).  This is the\nsign the *multiplicative* pairwise route provably cannot supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L74-L82","doc":"**Strictly below `1` for `h ≠ 0`** (the physical regime `q ≠ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**The Borromean trace lies at or below the unlink value `1`** for every real\n`h`.  (`h⁴ ≥ 0`, `3 + h² > 0`, `h² + 4 > 0` ⇒ the deficit `≥ 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.one_sub_tauBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.one_sub_tauBorromean","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**Trace-deficit closed form.**  `1 − τ_Borr = h⁴(3 + h²)/(h² + 4)`.  This is\nthe irreducible 3-body content: the Borromean trace measured against the unlink\n`τ(0) = 1`.  (Being Brunnian, no pairwise part is subtracted — it vanishes.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L51-L53","doc":"The 3-component unlink is `τ_Borr(0) = 1` (writhe-0 trivial eigenvalue). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tauBorromean","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.lean#L46-L49","doc":"The Borromean `H₃` Markov-trace closed form (GAP-A-4,\n`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace`), as a function of `h = q − q⁻¹`:\n`τ_Borr(h) = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶)/(h² + 4)`.  Amphichiral ⇒ even in `h`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}